<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#caravanserai">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Caravanserai</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A caravanserai is a roadside inn built around a courtyard, providing lodging for travellers and their animals along trade routes in the Islamic world. Caravanserais supported long-distance commerce by offering safety, storage and services. They were built in cities and along routes by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a>, among others.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/caravanserai.jpg" alt="Caravanserai" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bernard Gagnon · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Izadkhvast_Caravanserai_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
